      "title": "ASP vs Kafka Connector vs Flink",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Decision rule: If you're already on Atlas and need real-time processing without operating infrastructure, use ASP. Use Kafka Connector when you need MongoDB as a source/sink in an existing Kafka ecosystem. Use Flink for complex stateful computation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-atlas-stream-processing/#asp-vs-kafka-connector-vs-flink",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
